James sought guidance on organizing his extensive collection of academic PDFs, which had become scattered across multiple folders. I recommended a structured approach, including creating a central repository, utilizing a reference manager like Zotero or Mendeley, and implementing a consistent naming convention. Later, James expressed interest in using Mendeley but faced issues accessing PDFs due to moving their locations. I informed him about Mendeley's cloud storage capabilities, detailing steps to sync his library, upload PDFs, and utilize organizational features within the application. Additionally, I suggested backup options and alternatives for external syncing to ensure his research documents remained accessible and secure.
